model {
  extend basalt.build {
    metadata {
      constraint "The plan-loader overlay applies after carries that add central scenarios, preserving their insertion context. Adopted scenarios declare their exact fixtures, applicability and CI groups beside each test. Preparation and source verification derive the same typed overlay, and coverage rejects missing plans, drift and scheduled targets without a runner. Input patterns must match frozen source or carried targets, including supported unified patches. Undeclared executable inputs and shared E2E helpers select the full suite and all declaration matrices; area heuristics cannot establish coverage. Automatic declared Cloud assignments reject specs that import serverControl directly or through scenario helpers; existing explicit Cloud jobs retain their target-aware fixtures. Declarations carry required pool-setup and catalog-route fixtures into automatic runs. The catalog-route source uses a reserved placeholder replaced before serving, so full-origin and hostname replacements cannot overlap. Deferred parity failures remain named not-run targets with their issue, including Cloud-only scenarios without a self-host substitute. Preparation removes the obsolete Rules draft journey after all carries and keeps its removed plan out of runtime selection. Approved-mock checks accept a computed selector only when shell double quotes execute the verified declaration command."
    }
  }
}
